totals sums over the sampled chunk-rows. Informational fields never fail the check:

cells_compared (informational): sampled SOURCE rows × Analyses. It excludes inserted TARGET rows, which inserted_rows counts, so it is comparable across spans.
parent_observed (informational): the sampled SOURCE cells with finite Z and SE.
inserted_rows (informational): the inserted TARGET rows (not mapped from any SOURCE row) in the sampled spans.
missing_now_imputed (informational): source-missing cells that TARGET holds finite and flagged imputed, which is what completion is for.
parent_rows_without_finite (informational): sampled SOURCE rows with no observed cell.
Failing, each over the sampled cells: z_mismatch, se_mismatch, eaf_mismatch (a source-observed cell whose decoded value differs, NaN equal to NaN); observed_marked_imputed; observed_missing_in_child; missing_became_observed (a source-missing cell observed with imputed == 0); inserted_observed_cells; imputed_mask_invalid (an imputed value outside 0 and 1); z_se_missingness_mismatch (a cell, in SOURCE or TARGET, with only one of Z and SE finite).

A nonzero failing counter, parent_rows_unmapped &gt; 0, an order that is not preserved, and differing Analyses each fail the check (failures names parent_rows_unmapped, order_not_preserved, analyses_mismatch, or the counter). After an axis or Analyses failure the sample is skipped (bands_checked is 0) and the verdict says why.
Exit codes. 0 pass; 1 the check ran and found a mismatch (the verdict is still written, and each failure is named on stderr); 2 refused: nothing was checked, so no verdict is written and the reason is on stderr. Refused are a mixed-layout pair, a layout the check does not support (it checks Dense, Hybrid and Ragged pairs), a SOURCE that is not Observed-Only, a TARGET that is not Reference-Completed, a release that cannot be opened, a TARGET with no imputed mask, a release whose z plane and variant axis disagree in length or are empty.
Hybrid scope. A Hybrid pair (issue #295) is an Observed-Only Hybrid SOURCE and the complete-hybrid output made from it. Completion changes both components: it completes the Dense Component, folds each SOURCE Overflow association at a variant the LD panel added to the Dense axis into the Dense Component as an observed cell (imputed == 0), and rebuilds the Overflow on the completed shared axis without it (a crossover, issue #99). So the check compares the observed view across both components, by ALID:

Axes, exhaustively. The Dense Components’ axes and the shared axes are each mapped as above, and every TARGET Dense row must be on TARGET’s shared axis.
Every crossover. complete-hybrid records none, so they are derived from the axes: a SOURCE Overflow association whose ALID is a TARGET Dense row. Each must be an observed Dense cell, not marked imputed, whose decoded Z, SE and EAF equal the SOURCE value encoded and decoded with the TARGET Dense Component’s own codec: Z, then EAF against that row’s eaf_baseline, then SE against that EAF, as the fold writes it. A crossover is coded against the Dense Component’s baseline, not the Overflow’s, so bit-identity with SOURCE is not the rule; the round trip is exact, and a moved or altered value still differs from it. Every crossover is read, so the cost grows with the TARGET chunk-rows that hold one.
The Dense Component, sampled. The chunk-row sample above, over the two Dense Components, with the crossover cells on inserted rows set aside for the crossover check: they are the only observed, unflagged cells an inserted row may hold.
The Overflow, sampled. --n-random Analyses (all of them when there are fewer), drawn with their own numpy.random.default_rng(--seed). Every association of each is matched with TARGET’s by shared-axis ALID, in both directions, and must have bit-identical decoded Z, SE and EAF. SOURCE crossovers are left to the crossover check, and TARGET associations at a Dense variant to observed_in_both.
The Overflow, every Analysis. TARGET’s Overflow holds SOURCE’s association count less that Analysis’s crossovers, none of them at a TARGET Dense variant and none marked imputed.

The verdict carries "layout": "hybrid", then seed, n_random, source, target and analyses as above; analyses.identical also needs both Overflows to have one offset per Analysis.







