The check does not compare TARGET’s source_release_id with SOURCE’s release_id: a wrong pairing fails the axis or cell checks.


check-observed-view SOURCE TARGET --seed N --output verdict.json --ld-panel DIR [--ancestry EUR] [--n-random 1000] also checks an Observed-Only Ragged release SOURCE against the complete-ragged output TARGET (issue #296). A Ragged release has no grid to sample, and completion rebuilds the union variant axis, so every comparison is by variant identity (ALID), never by index. The exit codes, the required --seed and the verdict’s seed, n_random, source, target, analyses, failures, passed and seconds are those of the Dense check.

Axis. The exact SOURCE -&gt; TARGET ALID map of the Dense check; an unmapped source variant (parent_rows_unmapped) or differing Analyses fail the check and skip the sample. Order is not required: axis.order_preserved is reported, not failed, because the associations are compared by ALID.
Sample. Whole Analyses, each compared completely: --n-random drawn uniformly with numpy.random.default_rng(--seed) (a store with fewer is sampled whole), plus the strata non_admitted (every Analysis the ancestry filter did not admit, up to 100, drawn with default_rng((seed, 1)) beyond that), largest (the 5 with most associations), empty (up to 5 with none) and trait_less (the first 5 without a Trait position). An Analysis is not admitted when its TARGET completed_against is empty (ADR 0028).
Per Analysis. Each source-observed association (finite Z and SE) is in TARGET with identical decoded Z, SE and EAF (NaN equal to NaN) and imputed == 0; TARGET holds no association with finite Z and SE and imputed == 0 that SOURCE lacks (target_observed_not_in_source); every imputed value is 0 or 1; every imputed association lies inside one of the Analysis’s retained regions; a non-admitted Analysis holds no imputed cell (imputed_in_non_admitted). Rows that are neither observed nor imputed (NaN: panel positions inside a region that completion could not fill) are counted as nan_rows and fail nothing.
Retained regions need the LD panel. A release stores no region coordinates, only block ids and counts in completion_quality; block extents live in the panel. The check rebuilds each sampled admitted Analysis’s blocks as complete-ragged chose them (ADR 0014, ADR 0039): the blocks touching its Trait position plus or minus the manifest’s provenance.completion.cis_window_bp, or, with no Trait position, the blocks holding enough of its own observations; a region is the panel positions of those blocks. --ld-panel (the directory complete-ragged was given) is therefore required for a Ragged pair, and --ancestry must equal provenance.completion.ancestry when given. There is no panel-free fallback. A completion_quality block the rebuilt regions lack is quality_blocks_not_in_regions, so a panel other than the one used is noticed. --ld-panel for a Dense or Hybrid pair is refused.
Totals. observed_in_source, imputed, nan_rows and regions (retained Analysis-by-block regions) are informational. Failing: z_mismatch, se_mismatch, eaf_mismatch, observed_marked_imputed, observed_missing_in_target, target_observed_not_in_source, imputed_outside_retained, imputed_in_non_admitted, imputed_mask_invalid, z_se_missingness_mismatch, target_variants_unordered (an Analysis’s variant indices not strictly increasing) and quality_blocks_not_in_regions. sample lists each checked Analysis with its strata, admission, the ids of its retained blocks and counts, and by_stratum counts them.
Refused (exit 2): a mixed-layout pair, a Ragged pair without --ld-panel, an LD panel with no chromosomes for the ancestry, an ancestry other than the one recorded, a TARGET completed against an ancestry other than the panel’s, a TARGET with no completion ancestry or cis_window_bp recorded, a release that cannot be opened or decoded (a missing array group or EAF array included), and either --ld-panel or --ancestry for a Dense or Hybrid pair.
Known limit: residual-coded SE. SE is compared for exact equality, as the contract in section 12 states. Ragged completion refits se_coefficients over the completed Analysis, so when SE is int8_residual (ADR 0037 section 3) every observed SE of an Analysis that was completed is re-quantised and differs from its source (on three real Chen 2023 Analyses completed with --cis-window-bp 1000000: all 135,596 observed SE differ, by a median of 0.09% and at most 0.14%, with Z and EAF identical); such a pair fails with se_mismatch. Where SE is float16 the pair is exact. The check stays strict (owner ruling, 2026-10-22): the re-quantisation is completion’s defect, and opengwasdb#301 owns fixing the refit, not this check.
